{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1543288-help-with-supernatural-type","id":1543288,"title":"Help with supernatural type","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-07T15:23:03-07:00","id":1543288,"title":"Help with supernatural type","content":"Hello, I recently wrote a short story about a character I would like to find a best-fit supernatural type. The main character\u2019s friend is brutally murderer and she starts having recurring nightmares about a shadow creature that did the murder. As she investigates her friend\u2019s murder, she struggles with sleep. As time progresses, the nightmare shifts from being chased by the shadow creature to it taunting her. Finally, she falls asleep watching \u201cA Nightmare on Elm Street\u201d and the shadow speaks to her in Freddy Kruegers voice. She reaches out to touch the shadow creature, but touches a mirror, the shadow disappears and she wakes. <br /> <br /> What supernatural type would be a best fit for this character? I plan to do more with her as an NPC in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24791-immortal","name":"Immortal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-07T18:17:09-07:00","id":1543303,"title":"","content":"Slasher probably works best. Could be an urged moving towards possessed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T04:30:54-07:00","id":1543331,"title":"","content":"Where would I find the information on those? I am not familiar with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24791-immortal","name":"Immortal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T15:23:22-07:00","id":1543362,"title":"","content":"Slasher is in a supplement called, well, Slasher.<br /> <br /> Urged is just someone being spirit-ridden, the rules are in the corebook, although I remember there being a 1st ed book about the Shadow that contains useful info/fluff.<br /> <br /> If you want to make the dream stuff into something the creature is manifesting on purpose, then maybe Changeling, but I think Slasher or Urged do work very well here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T17:15:44-07:00","id":1543372,"title":"","content":"Question are you talking about the thing taunting the NPC, or did something happen and now the NPC is no longer a baseline human?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T17:26:25-07:00","id":1543373,"title":"","content":"Slashers are from Hunter the Vigil if you're using 2nd edition or the Slasher book in 1st edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T19:49:15-07:00","id":1543382,"title":"","content":"I appreciate the responses, I\u2019ll be looking into the PDF for those types.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24791-immortal","name":"Immortal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T03:40:52-07:00","id":1543410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Immortal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1543288-help-with-supernatural-type#post1543288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello, I recently wrote a short story about a character I would like to find a best-fit supernatural type. The main character\u2019s friend is brutally murderer and she starts having recurring nightmares about a shadow creature that did the murder. As she investigates her friend\u2019s murder, she struggles with sleep. As time progresses, the nightmare shifts from being chased by the shadow creature to it taunting her. Finally, she falls asleep watching \u201cA Nightmare on Elm Street\u201d and the shadow speaks to her in Freddy Kruegers voice. She reaches out to touch the shadow creature, but touches a mirror, the shadow disappears and she wakes.<br /> <br /> What supernatural type would be a best fit for this character? I plan to do more with her as an NPC in the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would work very well also with a Beast, an Eshmaki in particular.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}